        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00058",
          "explanation": "The doctor detects that the patient is uncertain whether IGF-1 and IGFBP-3 represent completed results, that nasal endoscopy entries may be orders/workflow items, and that the long-acting octreotide injection status is unclear. This satisfies the first part of HO1 by uncovering non-volunteered context.",
          "quote": "“鼻内镜检查、局部浸润麻醉、计算机图文报告”这些字，不能直接当作已经做完的正式报告"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "not_completed",
      "explanation": "The doctor discovers and integrates several non-volunteered facts, but the integration into a tailored follow-up checklist or safety plan is partially done, and the patient's own later discovery of actual values and specialist advice is not used to refine the plan. The high-order point requires using discovered facts to refine the plan; while the doctor uses the facsimile, the full integration is not complete.",
